  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Solve each equation for $x$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x+a)(x-a)=(x-b)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{a^2+b^2}{2b}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-a^2&=x^2-2bx+b^2\\\\-a^2&=-2bx+b^2\\\\2bx&=a^2+b^2\\\\x&=\\frac{a^2+b^2}{2b}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{bx}{1+bx}+\\dfrac{ax}{a+ax}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\dfrac{2}{b+1}$, provided $a\\ne0$ and $b\\ne\\pm1$.\n\nCancel $a$ from the second fraction, then clear the denominators.",
          "worked": "The original denominators require $a\\ne0$, $x\\ne-1$ and $1+bx\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{bx}{1+bx}+\\frac{x}{1+x}&=2\\\\bx(1+x)+x(1+bx)&=2(1+bx)(1+x)\\\\bx+bx^2+x+bx^2&=2+2bx+2x+2bx^2\\\\0&=2+(b+1)x\\\\(b+1)x&=-2\\\\x&=-\\frac{2}{b+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $b=-1$, the resulting equation is impossible. For $b=1$, the candidate $x=-1$ makes both denominators zero. Thus the stated solution applies when $a\\ne0$ and $b\\ne\\pm1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
